{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For I know.</b> I shall recite that song and testify against you that I knew you would act in a manner that brings evil upon you, so that you will not attribute what is to come to chance, but rather to your own corruption, and take heart to return. As it says: וָאַגִּיד לְךָ מֵאָז, בְּטֶרֶם תָּבוֹא הִשְׁמַעְתִּיךָ, פֶּן תֹּאמַר עָצְבִּי עָשָׂם (Isaiah 48:5)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:50.649396446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}